Description: iOS MCP 1.2.8, packaged for shivtools
 An MCP server that runs inside SpringBoard, so an agent can read the
 screen, the view hierarchy and the live system log, drive the UI, and
 install IPAs from the device itself. Upstream is witchan/ios-mcp; this
 is the same code with two changes and a different package name.
 .
 What is different here:
 .
 - The server listens on 127.0.0.1 by default. Upstream binds
   INADDR_ANY, which exposes an unauthenticated server to everyone on
   the network. Network mode is still one setting away; from a Mac the
   cheaper route is an SSH tunnel, which costs nothing and gives
   authentication and encryption for free.
 - mcp-root is installed WITHOUT the setuid bit. With it set, any
   process on the device can become root through the helper's own
   allow-list. Turn it on deliberately with: shiv-mcp root-ac
 .
 Neither is a lock: both are settings, and the responsibility is the
 developer's. They are defaults, not walls.
 .
 The PaddleOCR engine, its two models and the IPA chain (AppSync,
 appinst, ldid, roothelper) are all included; nothing is downloaded on
 install.
 .
 Installing or upgrading this package loads a new SpringBoard dylib.
 RESPRING IS REQUIRED and it is not done for you.
